Caveats: 
  * N_GON controls the polygon type.  Set it at the top of 
    Section 0 to study triangles (3), squares (4), pentagons 
    (5), hexagons (6), heptagons (7), etc. 
  * For n in {3,4,6} the tiling closes flat (deficit=0); the 
    sheet structure is driven entirely by the tau rule. 
  * Deeper BFS (depth 6, xhuge preset) gives ~thousands of 
    cells; dimension fits are improved but still finite-size. 
  * TAU_MODE controls whether the main cluster uses the 
    didactic every-n rule, the signed-n rule (richer monodromy), 
    or the rigorous cut-and-project window of idea.md §2.4. 
  * KPM spectral analysis (Section 18) is the preferred 
    method for large clusters where dense eigendecomposition 
    is infeasible.  Both low-lambda slope and integrated-DOS 
    slope are reported for cross-validation. 
  * Same-orientation tiling is geometrically frustrated; this 
    experiment lets the sheet index absorb the angular deficit, 
    consistent with the multi-sheeted construction. 
